# Retire

Retire content when the feature it describes has gone, or when it is wrong and cannot be fixed. Do not leave it online with a warning.

## Point people to what replaced it

Link the old page to the new one. If nothing replaces it, say so and say what the person can do.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Page not found. | This help has moved to [Heating schedules](#). |
| This feature is no longer supported. | The motion light feature was removed in version 2026.9. Use an automation with a motion trigger instead. |

## Keep the old name where saved settings need it

A saved automation may still use an old key. Do not rename it in documentation unless a tested migration changes it. Explain the old name beside the new one.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Services are now actions. | The interface now says “action”. Older instructions and some saved files say “service”. They mean the same thing. |

## Record what you retired

Write a [change note](../writing-guidelines/change-notes.html) saying what was removed, when, and where to go instead.
